# ── Local secrets & operator config — NEVER commit (see CLAUDE.md) ──
.env
.env.*
# Templates are safe to track (no leading slash: applies at every depth,
# e.g. .env.example, deploy/.env.example) — they document non-secret
# defaults, never real values. Re-ignore patterns below: *.token, *.vault,
# secrets*.json/yml, *.local.json/yml (never match ".example", so this
# negation can't reopen them) and vault-pass* (deliberate exception: it
# DOES still shadow vault-pass.example, because a vault-pass file's whole
# content is the password — there is no non-secret default to template).
# It cannot reach inside a fully-ignored directory (/config/, dev/local/)
# — that is a known git limitation, not a gap in this pattern.
# ORDERING IS LOAD-BEARING: any secret pattern added ABOVE !*.example is
# punched through by it. New secret patterns go BELOW this line.
!*.example
*.token
*.vault
vault-pass*
secrets*.json
secrets*.yml
# Anchored to the repo root (leading slash) — this ignores only a top-level
# operator-config mount (e.g. a root config/ directory), matching the intent
# in CLAUDE.md's "dev/local/, .env, config/" list. Without the leading
# slash, git matches "config/" at ANY depth, including inside application
# source (e.g. frontend/src/screens/config/) — silently dropping real
# source files from `git status`/`git add`. See issue #254. Do not remove
# the leading slash.
/config/
# Issue #844: the epic's (#841) persistent local-state location for
# file-backed secrets (deploy/config/secrets/) and operator TLS
# (deploy/config/tls/) -- deliberately a SEPARATE anchored entry from the
# legacy /config/ rule above, not a rename of it. Removing the legacy
# /config/ rule/convention is #845's job, not this one's -- both stay
# ignored side by side until that migration lands.
/deploy/config/
dev/local/
*.local.json
*.local.yml
# Issue #28: deploy/scripts/keycloak-realm-import.sh's scratch copy of a
# realm export with a REAL client secret substituted in (never the
# committed deploy/keycloak/realm/waypoint-realm.json placeholder) -- see
# that script's header comment for why it lives under deploy/ rather than
# /tmp. Anchored: only the one script-owned directory, not a generic name.
/deploy/.keycloak-import-scratch/

# Certificates & keys
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12

# Build output
# Audited #362 (follow-up to #254, which anchored config/ -> /config/ after
# it swallowed frontend/src/screens/config/ as app source): every pattern
# below is intentionally LEFT unanchored. Each is a build-tool-owned
# directory name (.NET bin/obj, npm node_modules/dist, pytest/dotnet-test
# TestResults, CPython __pycache__) that legitimately recurs at every
# nesting depth (e.g. backend/*/bin/, frontend/vite-plugins/dist/) and,
# unlike "config", is never a plausible name for a hand-written source
# directory - confirmed by `find` across backend/ and frontend/src/ turning
# up no such collisions. Anchoring any of these to root would MISS the
# nested build output they exist to ignore. Do not anchor without re-
# confirming a real collision first.
bin/
obj/
TestResults/
node_modules/
dist/
frontend/build/
# Python bytecode from the sanitize scanner and its test suite
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor/OS noise
.vscode/
.instructions/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp
